/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
274 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 210 0 R
/E (In response to the evolving threat landscape and the dissolution of the traditional network perimeter, modern enterprises are rapidly shifting away from legacy VPN-centric remote access models. These conventional approaches often grant excessive network-level access, creating a significant attack surface and increasing the risk of lateral threat movement. To address these challenges, this project centers on the implementation of a Zero Trust security architecture, fundamentally operating on the principle of "never trust, always verify." By moving beyond location-based access, we aim to establish a security posture where trust is no longer implicit, and access is determined by granular context rather than network connectivity. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
