/T (Scenario 3: Executive Access to Confidential Board Documents A company executive needs to access a confidential folder containing board meeting materials hosted on an  internal file server. The executive connects from a tablet device while traveling internationally. ZPA integrates  with the mobile device management \(MDM\) solution to verify that the tablet is compliant \(not jailbroken,  passcode enabled, encryption active\). Upon successful authentication, ZPA evaluates the policy: "If user is in  'Executive_Board' group AND device is MDM-compliant AND connection is from a trusted country  \(allowlist\), THEN grant access to 'Board_Documents' application." The executive is connected directly to the  specific file share, and all data in transit is encrypted via TLS. Any attempt to access other shares or network  resources is automatically blocked and logged.  Output: )
/E (Scenario 3: Executive Access to Confidential Board Documents A company executive needs to access a confidential folder containing board meeting materials hosted on an  internal file server. The executive connects from a tablet device while traveling internationally. ZPA integrates  with the mobile device management \(MDM\) solution to verify that the tablet is compliant \(not jailbroken,  passcode enabled, encryption active\). Upon successful authentication, ZPA evaluates the policy: "If user is in  'Executive_Board' group AND device is MDM-compliant AND connection is from a trusted country  \(allowlist\), THEN grant access to 'Board_Documents' application." The executive is connected directly to the  specific file share, and all data in transit is encrypted via TLS. Any attempt to access other shares or network  resources is automatically blocked and logged.  Output: )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [12]
>>
