/T (external collaborators in the identity provider with limited attributes. ZPA policies are created that specifically grant the "Acquired_HR" group access only to the "Benefits_App" \(a web application hosted internally\). The acquired users install the ZPA client, authenticate, and are connected directly to the benefits application. Because ZPA provides access without network connectivity, the parent company's entire internal network remains completely hidden and protected. The acquired users cannot ping, scan, or access any other corporate resource. After six months, when the integration is complete and users are migrated to the parent identity system, the temporary policies are revoked.  Output: )
