/Title (Scenario 4: IT Administrator Access to Server Management Interfaces  A systems administrator requires access to management interfaces \(SSH for Linux servers and RDP for  Windows servers\) to perform routine maintenance. Instead of granting VPN access to the entire management  network, ZPA is configured to treat each server or management interface as a separate application segment. The  administrator authenticates and is presented only with the specific servers they are authorized to manage based  on their IT subgroup \(e.g., "Linux_Admins" see only Linux servers; "Windows_Admins" see only Windows  servers\). When the admin connects via SSH to a Linux server, ZPA creates a direct micro-tunnel to that specific  IP and port combination. The admin cannot scan the subnet, access other servers, or initiate connections to  non-authorized ports.)
